---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Acceptable Use Policy"
  description="Guidelines for responsible self-hosted operation and creator clipping."
  currentPath="/acceptable-use"
  section="Legal"
>
  <h2>1. Respect Creator &amp; Platform Rules</h2>
  <p>
    Only clip, remix, or republish content from creators whose guidelines permit clipping, or where
    you hold explicit permission or applicable fair-use rights. Always credit original creators
    where required.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Prohibited Uses</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Using ClipCut to automate spam, harassment, impersonation, or unauthorized re-uploads.</li>
    <li>Circumventing platform rate limits, access controls, or OAuth API restrictions.</li>
    <li>Deploying public multi-user instances without appropriate rate limits and account verification.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Server Operator Controls</h2>
  <p>
    Administrators running public instances should enable accounts (<code>CLIPCUT_ACCOUNTS=1</code>),
    email verification (<code>CLIPCUT_VERIFY_EMAIL=1</code>), and sensible per-user limits in{" "}
    <code>.env</code>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
